## Headings and spacing

- Use a single H1 (`#`) per document for the page title.
- Use `##` and `###` for sections and subsections.
- Insert one blank line before and after headings and lists.
- Keep lines readable; wrap long lines thoughtfully but avoid unnecessary reflows.

## Lists and text

- Use `-` for unordered lists; keep bullet style consistent.
- Favor short, scannable sentences and concrete examples.

## Code fences and dialogues

- Always specify a language on code fences. Common: `text`, `markdown`, `mermaid`, `bash`, `yaml`.
- Use `text` fences for conversations or transcripts.
- Use `mermaid` fences for diagrams.

## Links and media

- Prefer relative links; avoid bare URLs in prose.
- When linking media, ensure the target exists under `media/` and previews on GitHub.
- Provide clear link text; avoid “click here”.

## File endings and whitespace

- End every file with a single trailing newline.
- Avoid trailing spaces and mixed indentation.

## Optional footer

- You may include a final line: `File location: \`path/to/file\`` (exact path in backticks).

## Tone and voice

- Persona voice only in persona-facing docs (see persona-voice-and-tone rules).
- Neutral, professional tone in all other documentation.
